d","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::9e3be59865b2c1c335d32dae2fe7b254","value":"Datacite"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"arXiv","value":"2310.11422"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3847/1538-4357/ad36c2"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Preprint","urls":["http://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11422"],"publicationDate":"2023-10-17","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::6f4922f45568161a8cdf4ad2299f6d23","value":"arXiv.org e-Print Archive"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::6f4922f45568161a8cdf4ad2299f6d23","value":"arXiv.org e-Print Archive"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3847/1538-4357/ad36c2"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doaj.org/article/fbc9c545e1494f86ad100f0ed8bc2dc5"],"publicationDate":"2024-01-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::f5c883d7dea7cfa40d9bf7581df67fde","value":"The Astrophysical Journal"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"green":true,"inDiamondJournal":false,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Torlakovic, Enver","name":"Enver","surname":"Torlakovic","rank":1,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"New Model of Galactic Rotation Curves","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["A model of galactic rotation curves is derived from the Vacuum Energy Quantum Field (VEQF) framework,explaining flat rotation curves of spiral galaxies without invoking WIMPs, MOND, or cosmic expansion. Darkmatter is posited as exotic quarks forming a primordial gravitational scaffold. Baryonic matter, in a bulge-disk-arms structure, enhances rotational support via geometric shape factors. The predicted rotation curvefor NGC 3198 matches observations with an RMSE  of 12.37 km/s and final velocity of 156.5 km/s(observed:  155.3 km/s). The model aligns with the ~27% dark matter energy density and uses no freeparameters beyond physical mass distributions and geometric scales.","Python script for curve calculation an plotting is provided in the paper"],"publicationDate":"2025-07-31","publisher":"Zenodo","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":null,"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::a458b6161d951b1ec517cc522706eb8c","originalIds":["50|datacite____::a458b6161d951b1ec517cc522706eb8c","10.5281/zenodo.16625799","50|od______2659::a458b6161d951b1ec517cc522706eb8c","oai:zenodo.org:16625799","50|datacite____::ddab732f79900549ab8f9e9cdfacf862","10.5281/zenodo.16625798"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5281/zenodo.16625799"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5281/zenodo.16625798"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.2497804E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":[{"code":"eosc","label":"EOSC","provenance":null}],"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::9e3be59865b2c1c335d32dae2fe7b254","value":"Datacite"},{"key":"opendoar____::358aee4cc897452c00244351e4d91f69","value":"ZENODO"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5281/zenodo.16625799"}],"license":"CC BY","type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16625799"],"publicationDate":"2025-07-31","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::358aee4cc897452c00244351e4d91f69","value":"ZENODO"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::9e3be59865b2c1c335d32dae2fe7b254","value":"Datacite"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5281/zenodo.16625799"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"oai","value":"oai:zenodo.org:16625799"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://zenodo.org/records/16625799","http://dx.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16625799"],"publicationDate":"2025-07-31","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::358aee4cc897452c00244351e4d91f69","value":"ZENODO"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::358aee4cc897452c00244351e4d91f69","value":"ZENODO"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.5281/zenodo.16625798"}],"license":"CC BY","type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16625798"],"publicationDate":"2025-07-31","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::358aee4cc897452c00244351e4d91f69","value":"ZENODO"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::9e3be59865b2c1c335d32dae2fe7b254","value":"Datacite"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"green":true,"inDiamondJournal":false,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::a911410dfe1ce42405b1ab769fa82bdd","fullName":"M. Khademi","name":"M.","surname":"Khademi","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-2865-0692"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"S. Nasiri","name":"S.","surname":"Nasiri","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"F. S. Tabatabaei","name":"F. S.","surname":"Tabatabaei","rank":3,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Dynamical Effect of Galactic Magnetic Fields on the HI Gas Rotation Curve","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Magnetic fields are known to influence the thermal and structural properties of galactic gas, yet their impact on the rotational dynamics of galaxies remains largely underexplored. In this study, we examine how the magnetic arms of the spiral galaxy NGC 6946 affect its HI-traced circular gas rotation, incorporating two dark matter density models: the pseudo-isothermal (ISO) and the Navarro-FrenkWhite (NFW) profile. To assess the magnetic contribution, we employ a three-dimensional representation of the galaxy’s magnetic field and perform a χ 2 minimization to match the modeled rotation curve with observational data. Our results show that including magnetic effects yields a better fit to the HI rotation curve, particularly in the outer disk where magnetic forces become more significant. The typical amplitude of the regular magnetic field contribution to the rotation curve increases with galactocentric radius, reaching approximately 14 km s−1 in the outer gaseous disk of the galaxy NGC 6946, which corresponds to about five percent of the observed rotational velocity. These findings suggest that largescale magnetic fields play a non-negligible role in the global dynamics of spiral galaxies, especially at large radii.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2026-01-07","publisher":"National Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Armenia","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Communications of the Byurakan Astrophysical Observatory","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2579-2776","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"427","vol":"72","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::d119896f78970992b7c55152433be87a","originalIds":["10.52526/25792776-25.72.2-427","50|doiboost____|d119896f78970992b7c55152433be87a"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.52526/25792776-25.72.2-427"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.6085654E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Institute for Research in Fundamental Sciences","acronym":"IPM","id":"openorgs____::48aaade15b9cff47d5871a7bf8d25140","pids":[{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006115"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/04xreqs31"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006116"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006115"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q6039681"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"1299267"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000088417951"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006116"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q6039681"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.418744.a"}],"countries":[{"code":"IR","label":"Iran (Islamic Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.ipm.ac.ir/"},{"legalName":"Shahid Beheshti University","acronym":"SBU","id":"openorgs____::4e7a193a2ea405eea82bb924cd0b7496","pids":[{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0091vmj44"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q609586"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q4116835"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"48379061"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100020481"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"24665789"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.412502.0"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q4116835"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000106864748"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"1248359"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q609586"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100020481"}],"countries":[{"code":"IR","label":"Iran (Islamic Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://en.sbu.ac.ir/sitepages/home.aspx"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.52526/25792776-25.72.2-427"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.52526/25792776-25.72.2-427"],"publicationDate":"2026-01-07","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn__online::719c0f2ece955d214affbd64117984c6","value":"Communications of the Byurakan Astrophysical Observatory"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"green":false,"inDiamondJournal":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::a911410dfe1ce42405b1ab769fa82bdd","fullName":"M. Khademi","name":"M.","surname":"Khademi","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-2865-0692"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"S. Nasiri","name":"S.","surname":"Nasiri","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::86148aced09321f11175b7bdf97f1675","fullName":"F. S. Tabatabaei","name":"F. S.","surname":"Tabatabaei","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-0377-0970"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"QB460-466"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Galaxy dynamics"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Astrophysics of Galaxies (astro-ph.GA)"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Galaxy rotation curves"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"FOS: Physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Galaxy magnetic fields"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Astrophysics"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Astrophysics - Astrophysics of Galaxies"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Galaxy kinematics"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Influence of Magnetic Fields on the Gas Rotation in the Galaxy NGC 6946","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>                <jats:p>Magnetic fields can play an important role in the energy balance and formation of gas structures in galaxies. However, their dynamical effect on the rotation curve of galaxies is immensely unexplored. We investigate the dynamical effect of the known magnetic arms of NGC 6946 on its circular gas rotation traced in H <jats:sc>i</jats:sc>, considering two dark-matter mass-density models, ISO, and the universal NFW profile. We used a three-dimensional model for the magnetic field structure to fit the modeled rotation curve to the observed data via a <jats:italic>χ</jats:italic>                   <jats:sup>2</jats:sup> minimization method. The shape of the H <jats:sc>i</jats:sc> gas rotation curve is reproduced better including the effect of the magnetic field, especially in the outer part, where the dynamical effect of the magnetic field could become important. The typical amplitude of the regular magnetic field contribution in the rotation curve is about 6–14 km s<jats:sup>−1</jats:sup> in the outer gaseous disk of the galaxy NGC 6946. The contribution ratio of the regular magnetic field to the observed circular velocity and to dark matter increases with the galactocentric radius. Its ratio to the observed rotational velocity is about 5% and, to dark matter, is about 10% in the outer regions of the galaxy NGC 6946. Therefore, the large-scale magnetic fields cannot be completely ignored in the large-scale dynamics of spiral galaxies, especially in the outer parts of galaxies.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2023-03-01","publisher":"American Astronomical Society","embargoEndDate":"2022-05-01","sources":["Crossref","The Astrophysical Journal, Vol 945, Iss 1, p 36 (2023)"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"The Astrophysical Journal","issnPrinted":"0004-637X","issnOnline":"1538-4357","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"36","vol":"945","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::1a78114b3f21429be56cfd8a06fb6bc2","originalIds":["10.3847/1538-4357/acb99b","50|doiboost____|1a78114b3f21429be56cfd8a06fb6bc2","50|datacite____::df0f8dcc5bc0d76e72e2f5278ecd5cf2","10.48550/arxiv.2205.09069","50|od________18::0b9558149fde0a7c53bab84f4cd45a31","oai:arXiv.org:2205.09069","oai:doaj.org/article:f25705eaf47b454fa0f8f52a13e3ea48","50|doajarticles::ff22efc8bc136523d87bf64af1d109b5"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3847/1538-4357/acb99b"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.48550/arxiv.2205.09069"},{"scheme":"arXiv","value":"2205.09069"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpd